## Summary

**Goal:** Who?'s group page (`/groups/<id>`, now `/g/<id>`) said "Not here" for any group that wasn't a directory group (family/classroom/grade), one of the viewer's tags, or a list they run or are in, even though the data model's generated `href` sent every other group kind there (plain groups like Spelling Bee, `category` headings like Activities).

**Built:**
- `web/who/state.js`: `openGroup(name)` queries the group by id (when it matches `/^grp[0-9A-Za-z]{11}$/`, Loop's test) or slug, and keeps the row in a separate `opened` map, so it never joins the sidebar or Tags filter. `listAt(key)` reads `lists` or `opened`; `groupPath`, `groupKeyOf`, `loadMembers`, `tags.js` and `pages/list.js` use it. `app.js`'s group route looks a missing name up once, remembering it only after a successful answer (a reviewer caught that a failed request marked the group missing for good).
- `internal/db/link.go` `groupLinks`: the generated `href` no longer defaults to Who?. Events, activities and parties keep When/Team/Celebrate; families, classrooms and grades go to Who?; any other group gets its `loop_href`, blank where Loop has no page (categories, bands, crews, departments). `docs/dev.md`, the column description and `link_test.go`/`tools_test.go` follow.

**Decisions:** ian asked what the use case was. With `href` in mind, ian first wanted bare `href` removed entirely (path plus app-specific hrefs only); I got partway, then ian stopped me and chose to keep `href` (the default link Ask, MCP and search hand out) with a rule that never points at Who? for a group Who? didn't show before. The Who? page fix stays, so a group someone does reach there opens.

**Left out:** an on-page error when the lookup fails (stays blank, as member loading already does); a JS test (no JS harness in the repo); links for category headings (ian: never link them).

