## Decisions

### Should plain groups' page links (`href`) stay on Who?, which this task makes work, or move to Loop?

**Background.** Every GROUP row the data model returns carries `href`, its page link. `groupLinks` in `internal/db/link.go` builds it. Events go to When, activities to Team and parties to Celebrate. Every other kind goes to Who? at `/g/<slug or id>`: plain `group` lists, `category` headings, bands, crews and departments. The Helios MCP server and Ask put that `href` into Claude's answers, so it is the link people click when Claude names a group.

Before this task, Who?'s `/g/` page opened only directory groups and the viewer's own lists, so those links landed on "Not here". This branch makes Who? open any open group the viewer can see. The page fetches the group, then shows its members as directory cards. That fix is done and tested on the sample server.

The use case is narrow: links the system hands out. Loop already has its own page for plain groups (`loop_href`), but category groups get no Loop link.

**The same two groups under each option:**

| Group | Today on main | Keep this branch (Who?) | Point plain groups at Loop |
|---|---|---|---|
| Spelling Bee, `grp9AomK6zhG7r`, kind `group`, slug `spelling-bee` | `who.heliosian.com/g/spelling-bee` → "Not here" | same link, opens with members as directory cards | `loop.heliosian.com/g/spelling-bee` → Loop's email-list page |
| Activities, `grpdwsPcjueNqv`, kind `category`, no slug | `who.heliosian.com/g/grpdwsPcjueNqv` → "Not here" | same link, opens with title and "No matches." (a category has no members) | no Loop page; stays the Who? link, so this branch is still needed, or the group gets no link |

- (*) Keep this branch as is
  One rule covers every kind: any group whose link goes to Who? opens there. No change to `link.go`. Plain groups show as directory cards rather than Loop's list page.
- ( ) Also point `href` at Loop for kind `group`
  A one-line change in `groupLinks`: kind `group` gets home `loop`. Spelling Bee's link opens Loop's page, where the list's address, posting rules and archive live. Categories, bands, crews and departments still go to Who?, so this branch's fix stays. That leaves two rules where there was one.

